[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3155227293","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109333#issuecomment-3155227293","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109333","id":3155227293,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc68EPKd","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-05T13:30:34Z","updated_at":"2025-08-05T13:30:34Z","body":"I've framed this as a discussion rather than a bug, since this has already applied to `--headless --export` for a long time now, and I figured the current behavior is \"by design\" anyway.\n\nAnyway, it would seem to me like the fix here is to just store the last inputs to `EditorNode::progress_task_step` along with a timestamp and only actually print the log message if either the task/step has changed or if some amount of time (like 1 second) has elapsed. That way it'll be apparent that the editor is still working on something and isn't completely frozen.\n\nI've put up such a PR here: #109334","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/31